
# editable-guard
- label: while a text-like input, textarea, select, or contenteditable is focused, typing / o j k g ? and a normal letter inserts those characters into the field
  id: edgtype
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'inserts those characters into the field' test/browser/editable-guard.test.js test/render/render-interactions-nav.test.js
  tags: [spec, editable-guard, implemented]
- label: rendered-session chapter j/k/o/Enter and slash-to-search do not run when any form field is focused, not only .filter-search
  id: edgnav
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'form field is focused|generic input|textarea, select, or contenteditable' test/render/render-interactions-nav.test.js test/browser/editable-guard.test.js
  tags: [spec, editable-guard, implemented]
- label: sessions filter, chapter search, run composer, rail filter, launch prompt and cwd, share token and repo, and session continue-form consume printable keys without slash-to-search, chapter toggle, peek step, or G-chord
  id: edgsurf
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'consume printable keys without|non-palette surfaces' test/browser/editable-guard.test.js
  tags: [spec, editable-guard, implemented]
- label: Enter on a .run-row does not navigate while a form field including .session-continue-input is focused
  id: edgent
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'Enter on a .run-row' test/browser/editable-guard.test.js
  tags: [spec, editable-guard, implemented]
- label: when no form field is focused, rendered-session slash still focuses chapter search and j/k still walk chapters
  id: edgidle
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "keydown '/' focuses filter search input|keydown 'j' focuses first visible chapter|keydown 'k' focuses last visible" test/render/render-interactions-nav.test.js
  tags: [spec, editable-guard, implemented]
- label: every document-level printable page shortcut (/ j k o G-chord) consults one shared GitHub isFormField; the bubble-phase keyDownHandler returns if isFormField(event.target) without stopPropagation so the event still reaches the field
  id: edg1
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "one shared GitHub isFormField|GitHub-style bubble-phase keyDownHandler" test/browser/is-form-field.test.js test/browser/editable-guard.test.js
  tags: [spec, editable-guard, implemented]
- label: Playwright page.keyboard.type("/ojkg?x") into the live composer #liveTailInput inserts those characters and does not slash-to-search, G-chord, or steal focus
  id: edglive
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "live composer #liveTailInput" test/browser/editable-guard.playwright.test.js
  tags: [spec, editable-guard, implemented]
- label: unscoped printable page shortcuts fire from one GitHub-style bubble-phase keyDownHandler that returns when isFormField(event.target) without stopPropagation so the keydown still reaches the focused field
  id: edgdisp
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "GitHub-style bubble-phase keyDownHandler|isFormField.event.target" test/browser/is-form-field.test.js test/browser/editable-guard.test.js
  tags: [spec, editable-guard, implemented]
- label: Playwright page.keyboard.type("/ojkg?x") on focused #liveTailInput keeps value /ojkg?x and each of those keydowns reaches the focused control
  id: edgreach
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "live composer #liveTailInput" test/browser/editable-guard.playwright.test.js
  tags: [spec, editable-guard, implemented]
- label: unscoped / o j k g fire from the one GitHub-style keyDownHandler via data-hotkey elements in the radix trie; they are not sibling document bubble listeners with a copied isFormField return
  id: edgreg
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "unscoped / o j k g fire from the one GitHub-style keyDownHandler via data-hotkey" test/browser/is-form-field.test.js test/browser/editable-guard.test.js
  tags: [spec, editable-guard, implemented]
- label: while #workspaceSearch is focused, typing / o j k g ? and a normal letter inserts those characters into the field
  id: edgws
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "inserts those characters into the field" test/browser/editable-guard.test.js
  tags: [spec, focus-seam, editable-guard, shortcut-when-idle, implemented]
- label: isFormField returns false unless the node is an HTMLElement (instanceof HTMLElement), matching GitHub
  id: edghtml
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "isFormField uses instanceof HTMLElement" test/browser/is-form-field.test.js
  tags: [github/hotkey, spec, editable-guard, implemented]
- label: the radix trie leaf fires a data-hotkey element only when (!formField && !scope) || (formField && target.id === scope); unscoped / o j k g do not run while a form field is focused even if a data-hotkey-scope node exists
  id: edgleaf
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "GitHub leaf filter" test/browser/is-form-field.test.js test/browser/editable-guard.test.js
  tags: [spec, editable-guard, implemented]
- label: Playwright page.keyboard.type("/ojkg?x") into focused #liveTailInput and Cmd+K #cmdkInput inserts those characters even when a data-hotkey-scope node is present
  id: edgleafpw
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "live composer #liveTailInput|#cmdkInput still gets|data-hotkey-scope node is present" test/browser/editable-guard.playwright.test.js
  tags: [spec, editable-guard, implemented]
- label: unscoped / o j k g are installed as data-hotkey HTMLElements in a GitHub radix trie, not a JS callback list on document
  id: edgtrie
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "radix trie of data-hotkey" test/browser/is-form-field.test.js test/browser/editable-guard.test.js
  tags: [spec, editable-guard, implemented]
- label: keyDownHandler walks the radix trie and on Leaf fire calls fireDeterminedAction then event.preventDefault
  id: edgprev
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "preventDefault on leaf fire|fireDeterminedAction then event.preventDefault" test/browser/is-form-field.test.js
  tags: [spec, editable-guard, implemented]
- label: Playwright page.keyboard.type("/ojkg?x") into focused #liveTailInput and Cmd+K #cmdkInput still inserts those characters with radix-trie dispatch
  id: edgtriepw
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "live composer #liveTailInput|#cmdkInput still gets|data-hotkey-scope node is present" test/browser/editable-guard.playwright.test.js
  tags: [spec, editable-guard, implemented]
- label: normalizeHotkey localizes Mod to Meta on Apple platforms and Control elsewhere, then sorts modifiers as Control, Alt, Meta, Shift
  id: edgnorm
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "normalizeHotkey localizes Mod and sorts modifiers" test/browser/is-form-field.test.js
  tags: [spec, editable-guard, github/hotkey, implemented]
- label: eventToHotkeyString encodes a keydown with GitHub modifier order, macOS Alt-symbol mapping, and macOS Command+Shift uppercase mapping
  id: edgenc
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "eventToHotkeyString applies GitHub macOS Alt-symbol and Command.Shift layers" test/browser/is-form-field.test.js
  tags: [spec, editable-guard, github/hotkey, implemented]
- label: G-then-letter jumps are declared as GitHub sequences g c, g r, g d, g v, and g n without four-way letter-case aliases
  id: edgseq
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "G-then-letter jumps are declared as GitHub sequences" test/browser/is-form-field.test.js test/browser/command-palette-nav.test.js test/browser/shortcut-when-idle.test.js
  tags: [spec, editable-guard, github/hotkey, implemented]
- label: Playwright page.keyboard.type(/ojkg?x) still inserts into #liveTailInput and #cmdkInput, and idle g then c or r still jumps, with GitHub sequence encoding instead of four-way case aliases
  id: edgseqpw
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "live composer #liveTailInput|#cmdkInput still gets|idle G then C/R/D/V/N jumps" test/browser/editable-guard.playwright.test.js test/browser/shortcut-when-idle.playwright.test.js
  tags: [spec, editable-guard, github/hotkey, implemented]
- label: keyDownHandler sequenceReset()s on unscoped form-field return so an idle g does not stay armed through typing; after blur, c does not complete g c
  id: edgreset
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "sequenceReset on form-field return" test/browser/is-form-field.test.js
  tags: [spec, editable-guard, github/hotkey, implemented]
- label: Playwright idle g then type in #liveTailInput then blur then c does not navigate to /; #liveTailInput still inserts /ojkg?x; idle g then c still jumps when no field is focused
  id: edgresetpw
